# pitch-probe.xrs - VR-173 prerequisite 1: does the ENGINE's own view pitch follow the
# head through a sword attack?
#
# Why it matters: the game aims a sword hit from its own view. The sibling BioShock mod
# wrote the rendered pitch from the head and discarded the engine's value, so the engine's
# pitch froze near straight down and melee landed on the floor while the picture looked
# right. If that fault exists here, anything that times or aims an attack from the
# physical blade inherits it.
#
# Needs: a loaded level in GAMEPLAY on the dev PC's sewer save, [Mode] GamepadOnly=0, the
# sword in the right hand (the first step draws it), and for leg 6 the pistol in the left
# hand with at least one shot.
# Run:   .\tools\xrsim-run.ps1 -Path .\tools\xrsim\pitch-probe.xrs -Dir <sim dir>
# Read:  python tools\pitch-probe-read.py <data dir>\dumps\camshake-p1-*.csv
#
# THE INSTRUMENT is the one VR-172 built: `camshake capture <s> <tag>` writes one row per
# game tick from the fresh branch of the head write, BEFORE the write: the pitch the
# engine handed in, the pitch the mod wrote on the previous tick, the controller's own
# rotation, the camera's, and the animation state. No new code runs for this measurement.
#
# WHY THE HEAD IS PITCHED. With the head level the head's pitch is 0, and an engine pitch
# frozen at 0 would agree with it perfectly. Legs 2 and 3 pitch the head 25 degrees up and
# down, where a frozen pitch reads as a 25 degree error. Leg 1 is the level reference.
#
# WHY LEG 6 IS HERE. An instrument that cannot print the unwelcome answer is not evidence.
# A pistol shot with the game's own kick allowed puts 2.84 degrees of pitch into the
# controller that the head did not write (VR-172); the same columns must show it.
#
# The attacks are `swing sim`: the simulator's display clock leaps about 135 ms across a
# game-thread hitch and cuts a simulated hand move short (TRAPS, VR-170).

hand r to grip 0.25 1.30 -0.40 0 0 0 1200
@wait 1500
trigger r pull 300
@wait 2500
@mod swing on; swing mode edge; swing threshold 3.0; swing rearm 1.0; swing cooldown 300; swing sword on; swing output rt; camshake on; camshake release all
@wait 1500

# 1. Level head, the shipped configuration.
head rot 0 0 0
@wait 1500
@mark
@mod camshake capture 5 p1-level; swing sim 5 200 3
@log swing: sim window finished: 3 fire 8s
@log camshake: CAPTURE 'p1-level' 10s

# 2. Head pitched 25 degrees UP.
head rot 0 25 0
@wait 1500
@mark
@mod camshake capture 5 p1-up25; swing sim 5 200 3
@log swing: sim window finished: 3 fire 8s
@log camshake: CAPTURE 'p1-up25' 10s

# 3. Head pitched 25 degrees DOWN.
head rot 0 -25 0
@wait 1500
@mark
@mod camshake capture 5 p1-down25; swing sim 5 200 3
@log swing: sim window finished: 3 fire 8s
@log camshake: CAPTURE 'p1-down25' 10s

# 4. The head MOVING through the attack: 25 down to 25 up over 1.2 s, the length of the
#    three swings. Retention is judged against the previous tick's write, so a moving
#    head does not count as an error; a lagging engine value would.
@mark
@mod camshake capture 5 p1-sweep; swing sim 5 200 3
head to 0 1.60 0 0 25 0 1200
@log swing: sim window finished: 3 fire 8s
@log camshake: CAPTURE 'p1-sweep' 10s

# 5. The game's own camera motion allowed (the master switch off), head 25 down: does an
#    attack add pitch of its own through an influence the mod normally holds at zero?
head rot 0 -25 0
@mod camshake off
@wait 2000
@mark
@mod camshake capture 5 p1-down25-gameshake; swing sim 5 200 3
@log swing: sim window finished: 3 fire 8s
@log camshake: CAPTURE 'p1-down25-gameshake' 10s

# 6. The control. The game's own camera motion allowed, one pistol shot: the capture MUST
#    show engine-added pitch (2.84 to 2.93 degrees, in the camera against the controller).
#    If this leg reads flat the instrument cannot see a divergence and legs 1 to 5 prove
#    nothing. It uses the MASTER switch and not `camshake allow fire on`: `allow` is written
#    to the ini, and a sequence that leaves the machine's own preferences changed has
#    altered the thing it was testing on (it did, once: TRAPS).
head rot 0 0 0
@mod camshake off
@wait 2000
@mark
@mod camshake capture 4 p1-control-kick
@wait 800
trigger l pull 200
@log camshake: CAPTURE 'p1-control-kick' .* controller rotation: pitch [1-9]\.\d\d\d yaw 8s

# Leave it as it was FOUND. The master switch is written to the ini too, so this line is
# what puts [CameraShake] Suppress back to 1, the shipped value; a machine that had it at 0
# has to be set back by hand, and a sequence that stops before this line leaves it at 0.
@mod camshake on; camshake status
head rot 0 0 0
hand r to grip 0.25 1.30 -0.40 0 0 0 1200
